-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Lunar Jetman
  Publisher   Ultimate, 1983
  Version     1.2

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Lunar Jetman (1983)(Ultimate Play The Game).z80
  MD5         4fd3f151dcf12216cb23618687da04d5

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Jetman in the suit of the Spec256 Jetpac; every alien family
              painted by its parts in its own colours; the moon rover in blue
              and cyan with dark grey tyres and light grey spokes. No white
              outlines or edges. Source: Jetman's Enhanced suit from an older
              Spec256 Jetpac conversion, painter not established.

  Pace        original (+0.37% measured in NexClash verifier replay pace: the
              same recording on both sides (the game takes its randomness from
              R, so JNext runs of two builds play different games), the hooks'
              added time at the Next's 28 MHz per game update (0x9ED2), 3
              recordings from the title)

  Changes     1.1: (never released) plays closer to the original's pace (about
              4% slow, was about 14%); the hooks hand back the CPU speed the
              game was running at
              1.2: plays within about half a percent of the original's pace;
              sprite images are shared between figures and uploaded only when
              no pattern holds them; the game's random numbers (taken from R)
              as the original's

  Note        The patch writes the whole alt ROM image (Sinclair's ROM plus
              its hooks), so the ROM's own interrupt code can never run the
              hooks. From 1.2 the figures and the rover share their sprite
              images, uploaded only when no pattern already holds them, and
              the hooks leave R as the original would, so the game's random
              numbers are the original's. Known issues: about 0.4% slower than
              the original (replay pace, the same game on both sides: +0.37%
              to +0.57% over three recordings, up to +1.8% in the quietest
              third of game updates); 1.0 was about 14% slower, the unreleased
              1.1 about 4%. Missing: the cheats are unplayed by a person; not
              reached in testing: the alien base, the missile's flight, the
              rover carrying items and later levels; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite fuel
   3  No enemies

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

