-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      1.2 played by the owner in JNext 1.1.104, 2026-11-07: approved;
              1.1 never released; 1.0 played by Jon Attree in JNext through
              the real loader, 2026-11-04

  Replay      IDENTICAL on 3 recordings from the title, 22,090 frames, default
              and Enhanced (1.2): at every hook call (155,561: h_new, h_tnew,
              h_clr, h_eo, h_teo, h_cls, h_msg) original and patched code run
              from the same state to the same point, registers with R and 48K
              memory compared (dead stack aside), slots 4 and 5 restored, the
              patched ROM modelled as the Next fills it (NextZXOS's ROM3
              first, then the build's writes); at all 21,398 IM 1 interrupts
              the alt ROM image's handler run against the original's, no hook
              code reached; at every interrupt outside the plot code each
              object's sprite ink equals the pixels its own XOR stores put on
              the original screen (35,595 object checks), palette offset equal
              to the object's colour at every draw, sprite attributes modelled
              through NEXTREG and port 0x57, patterns through 0x303B / 0x5B;
              the shared pattern pool checked full and churning (2,500 random
              calls over all 222 figure graphics and the rover frames, some
              hidden and shown again: every shown sprite shows its graphic's
              tiles); 15 of 15 negatives detected on the default and 8 of 8 on
              Enhanced (new: tile ids moved, a pattern reused while shown, R
              one off, a live instruction NOPed); every 32nd screen read
              checked from the read to the line routine's end against the
              original, registers with R and memory outside the bitmap equal;
              Enhanced tiles checked against their default tiles; the shipped
              build starts at the file's own decrypter, proven in the
              simulator to reach the verified start state apart from 16 bytes
              of ROM keyboard and frame variables and dead stack

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless through the real loader on a private copy
              of the NextZXOS v2.09 card (1.2, 2026-11-08): menu v1.2, loading
              screen, game selection, play with Jetman, aliens, items and the
              rover as sprites, game over and the Hall of Fame, default and
              Enhanced; /tmp/NEXCLASH.NEX equal to the bare build each time.
              Earlier (1.0, 2026-11-04): the alt ROM image dumped in JNext
              equals the modelled Sinclair-plus-hooks image; walking pace
              equal to the plain build

  Coverage    random play with infinite lives on 3 recordings: walking,
              flying, firing, aliens of the first levels, bombs, the rover
              moving and destroyed, the missile warning, game over and the
              Hall of Fame; not reached: the alien base, the missile's flight
              and destruction, bombing the base, the rover carrying items,
              later levels; cheats from the archive's POKEs for this release
              (its "Infinite Lives (corrected)" bytes, and fuel and no-enemies
              written for the rotated code), lives, fuel and no enemies held
              in the simulator on the original code, unplayed by a person;
              whole alt ROM image from 2026-11-04: the previous build differs
              only in the alt ROM fill (stub) and the image's low half

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
